# Generated, append-only registries: every blog post appends a uniquely-named
# entry, so two concurrent post PRs only ever *both add* distinct lines at the
# same anchor. `merge=union` makes git keep both sides instead of flagging a
# conflict, which is what lets the console auto-resolve post-PR merges
# (console/src/merge-resolve.ts `resolveConflictOnBranch`). It also fixes plain
# local/human merges and rebases of the same file.
#
# Scope this narrowly. Prose files must NEVER be union-merged: keeping both
# sides of two edits to the same paragraph silently publishes a mangled
# sentence. Only generated registries belong here.
tools/remotion/src/Root.tsx merge=union
